CVSign 3/3: training configuration from the paper

Why: configs/baseline.yaml is CorrNet's own recipe. CVSign's Implementation
Details change only: ResNet34 backbone; 70 epochs; learning rate reduced by
80% (x0.2, CorrNet's MultiStepLR gamma) at epochs 25 and 40. Batch size 2,
Adam, lr 1e-4, weight decay 1e-4 and the VAC/SMKD losses (ConvCTC 1, SeqCTC
1, Dist 25 at temperature 8, shared weight-normalised classifier) already
match. TLP's Cu/Cp weights come with TLP's decoder (cvsign-1 patch). The
dataset is PHOENIX14-T, the only in-scope corpus.
Applies to: CorrNet @ 5a361cc709ae8f697f4c9e23760e64c2daa8f744
---
diff --git a/configs/cvsign.yaml b/configs/cvsign.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8521ef9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/configs/cvsign.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+feeder: dataset.dataloader_video.BaseFeeder
+phase: train
+dataset: phoenix2014-T
+# dataset: phoenix14-si5
+num_epoch: 70
+work_dir: ./work_dir/cvsign/
+batch_size: 2
+random_seed: 0
+test_batch_size: 2
+num_worker: 10
+device: 0,1
+log_interval: 10000
+eval_interval: 1
+save_interval: 5
+# python in default
+evaluate_tool: sclite
+loss_weights:
+  SeqCTC: 1.0
+  # VAC
+  ConvCTC: 1.0
+  Dist: 25.0
+  # TLP lift-pooling regularisers (TLP configs/baseline.yaml)
+  Cu: 0.001
+  Cp: 0.001
+#load_weights: ''
+
+optimizer_args:
+  optimizer: Adam
+  base_lr: 0.0001
+  step: [ 25, 40]
+  learning_ratio: 1
+  weight_decay: 0.0001
+  start_epoch: 0
+  nesterov: False
+
+feeder_args:
+  mode: 'train'
+  datatype: 'video'
+  num_gloss: -1
+  drop_ratio: 1.0
+  frame_interval: 1
+  image_scale: 1.0  # 0-1 represents ratio, >1 represents absolute value
+  input_size: 224
+
+model: slr_network.SLRModel
+decode_mode: beam
+model_args:
+  num_classes: 1296
+  c2d_type: resnet34 #resnet18, mobilenet_v2, squeezenet1_1, shufflenet_v2_x1_0, efficientnet_b1, mnasnet1_0, regnet_y_800mf, vgg16_bn, vgg11_bn, regnet_x_800mf, regnet_x_400mf, densenet121, regnet_y_1_6gf
+  conv_type: 2
+  use_bn: 1
+  # SMKD
+  share_classifier: True
+  weight_norm: True
